td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>220</td><td>5.42</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>230</td><td>5.66</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>240</td><td>5.88</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>250</td><td>6.10</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>260</td><td>6.32</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>270</td><td>6.53</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>280</td><td>6.73</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>290</td><td>6.93</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>300</td><td>7.13</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>310</td><td>7.32</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>320</td><td>7.51</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\nRemarks:\n1. Where the length between perpendiculars is between the lengths specified in this table, the value shall be calculated by linear interpolation.\n2. For a ship whose length between perpendiculars exceeds 350 metres, the value shall be calculated by the following formula.\n3. 8.07 + 0.018 × (LPP − 350). Here, LPP means length between perpendiculars (metres).\n\n[Source graphic annotation: All 31 left-hand and 3 right-hand value pairs are preserved in their original order. The other right-hand cells remain blank. The original notes numbered 1, 2 and 3, including the formula appearing under number 3, are retained.]\n","metadata":{"author_method":"Exact held-source units translated or completed using explicitly recorded source/target spans; original official records remain unchanged. All new units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION and UNREVIEWED.","author_title_record":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1522_KR000068\\translations\\tonnage_rule\\en.title.json","sha256":"c897b8af8593e31fdc2f6cb0caef7bbf94c13d2953aacc9e1b32bc312a7cd2e9"},"author_unit_artifacts":[{"json":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1522_KR000068\\translations\\tonnage_rule\\en.units.parts\\annex-0